---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/Sections/PageHeader.astro";
import StaffList from "../components/Sections/StaffList.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Ariane Mader"
  seoTitle="About Ariane Mader | ADHD & Procrastination Coach"
  description="Meet Ariane Mader, an ADHD & procrastination coach with lived ADHD experience, coaching and counselling training, and a PhD in chemistry."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.arianemader.com/about"
  lang="en"
  alternateEn="https://www.arianemader.com/about"
  alternateDe="https://www.arianemader.com/de/about"
  xDefault="https://www.arianemader.com/about"
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Hi, I'm Ariane."
    subtitle="ADHD & Procrastination Coach, counsellor, and scientist at heart."
    backgroundImage="/uploads/about-header2.jpg"
    overlayOpacity={0.35}
  />

  <!-- Background & Training quick overview -->
<section class="py-6 bg-gray-50">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 text-center flex flex-col justify-center">
          <p class="font-[Cambria] font-bold text-lg mb-1">PhD in Chemistry</p>
          <p class="my-0 text-gray-700">
            Background in scientific research
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 text-center flex flex-col justify-center">
          <p class="font-[Cambria] font-bold text-lg mb-1">Coaching & Counselling</p>
          <p class="my-0 text-gray-700">
            Two-year training · 
            <a
              href="https://www.counselling.nl/en/"
              class="underline text-[#193472] hover:!text-[#30B28E]"
            >
              Academie voor Coaching en Counselling
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 text-center flex flex-col justify-center">
          <p class="font-[Cambria] font-bold text-lg mb-1">Confidential Advisor</p>
          <p class="my-0 text-gray-700">
            Professional training at </br>
            <a
              href="https://devertrouwenspersoon.nl/"
              class="underline text-[#193472] hover:!text-[#30B28E]"
            >
              De Vertrouwenspersoon
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 text-center flex flex-col justify-center">
          <p class="font-[Cambria] font-bold text-lg mb-1">Languages</p>
          <p class="my-0 text-gray-700">
            Coaching in English & German<br />
            Conversational Dutch
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

  <!-- About Me/Ariane -->
  <section class="pt-0 pb-8 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto prose prose-lg prose-max-w-none prose-p:my-3">
        <p>
          I’m originally from Germany and moved abroad to study chemistry. I went on to conduct scientific research and complete a PhD in chemistry.
          Along the way, I realized that some of the work I cared about most happened not in the lab, but in conversations:
          <b>helping people untangle a problem</b>, <b>understand themselves better</b>, and <b>find a way forward</b>.
          That led me to complete a two-year
          <a href="https://www.counselling.nl/en/trainings/coaching-and-counselling-english-year-2/"><u>Coaching & Counselling training</u></a>
          alongside my PhD, followed by training as a 
          <a href="https://devertrouwenspersoon.nl/opleiding/basisopleiding-vertrouwenspersoon/"><u>Confidential Advisor</u></a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          Coaching allows me to combine analytical thinking with creativity, curiosity, and a genuine interest in how people work.
          I work with people from a wide range of international backgrounds, coach in English and German, and also speak Dutch.
        </p>
        <!--I have now been coaching for three years; professional register LVSC?-->
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Full-bleed Personal Journey block (background reaches page edges even inside a container layout) -->
  <section class="bg-white py-8 w-screen relative left-1/2 right-1/2 -ml-[50vw] -mr-[50vw]">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
            <div class="prose prose-lg prose-max-w-none prose-p:my-3">
              <h2 class="blueFont font-[Cambria] text-2xl font-bold !mt-0 !mb-3">My Personal Journey</h2>
              <p>I was diagnosed with ADHD as an adult.</p>
              <p>
                Looking back, I can recognize many of the patterns much earlier in my life. 
                But especially during university and my PhD, when much of the external structure and pressure fell away, my struggle became difficult to ignore. 
                I had a hard time starting certain tasks, procrastinated a lot, and often relied on stress and last-minute pressure to get things done. 
                Because I performed well, things looked fine from the outside.
                But internally, it was exhausting.
              </p>
              <p>
                <b>What changed was not trying harder.</b> 
                I started treating my struggles more like an experiment: noticing patterns, trying different approaches, and gradually learning what helped me get started, follow through, and feel less stressed and frustrated.
                That learning process is still ongoing, but it has already fundamentally changed how I approach my work and everyday life.
              </p>
              <p>
                It also strongly influences the way I coach: with empathy, realism, and curiosity rather than judgement. 
                I know how frustrating it can be when something feels much harder than you think it should.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <img
                src="/uploads/me31.jpg"
                alt="Portrait of Ariane Mader, ADHD & Procrastination Coach"
                class="rounded-lg shadow-lg object-cover w-full max-w-sm md:ml-auto"
              />
            </div>
          </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How I Coach -->
  <section class="py-8 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto prose prose-lg prose-max-w-none prose-p:my-3">
        <h2 class="blueFont font-[Cambria] text-2xl font-bold !mt-0 !mb-3">How I Coach</h2>
        <p>People often describe me as calm, grounded, direct, and non-judgemental.</p>
        <p>
          In sessions, I aim to create a space that is supportive and honest at the same time. I may challenge you at times, but I will always respect your autonomy.
          You know your life best. My role is not to tell you what you should do, but to help you understand what is getting in your way and find <span class="greenDarkFont">approaches that genuinely work for you</span>.
        </p>
        <p>
          I don't expect one method to work for everyone. 
          We pay attention to what is happening, try things, and adjust. 
          <b>Every attempt gives us information. 
          An approach that does not work simply brings us closer to one that does.</b>
        </p>
        <p>
          Sometimes we work with practical tools such as planning, prioritizing, habits, and ways to lower the threshold for getting started.
          At other times, what is keeping you stuck may not be your planning system. 
          So we may look more closely at patterns, beliefs, expectations, perfectionism, fear, or other things that keep getting in your way.
        </p>
        <p>
          My goal is that over time, you <b>understand yourself better</b>, have <b>practical tools</b> you can actually use, and feel more <b>confident supporting yourself</b>.
        </p>
        <p>If this resonates with you, I’d be happy to explore working together.  <a
            href="/contact"
            class="underline hover:text-[#30B28E] transition-colors duration-200 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-primary-500 focus:ring-offset-2"
          >Book</a>
          a free intro call.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
